# Docker build context exclusions (backend / LavaLust).
#
# Render injects its own environment variables when the container starts.
# A .env that is baked into the image would be loaded by LavaLust on every
# request and would OVERRIDE those variables (putenv wins), which silently
# breaks CORS_ORIGIN, APP_ENV, JWT_SECRET, ... on the deployed site.

# ── Environment (never bake the real values into an image) ──────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── VCS / IDE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.idea
.vscode
*.sublime-*

# ── Runtime cache & logs (must stay writable at runtime) ───────────────
runtime/*
!runtime/.htaccess
!runtime/index.html
*.log
*.cache

# ── Docs / misc ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
README.md
changelog.md
LICENSE
